WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.530
Look at this ring of points.

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.350
A single straight line cannot

3
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.030
put the inside on one side and

4
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:08.290
the outside on the other.

5
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.610
Today: what one neuron can cut, and

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.510
why a stack with a bend can

7
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.330
separate a shape a line cannot.

8
00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.190
A neuron is a weighted sum, a

9
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.770
bias, and an activation.

10
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.840
The weights say how much each

11
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.560
input counts, and the bias shifts

12
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.360
the sum before the bend.

13
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.440
One neuron draws one straight cut.

14
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.570
Stack linear layers with no activation and

15
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.350
they collapse into that same single cut.

16
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.420
The activation is the bend.

17
00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.210
It lets the next layer turn the

18
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.950
previous cut into a curve.

19
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.560
Here is a ring.

20
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.540
A line misses it, and a small

21
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.140
network with a hidden layer

22
00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.340
learns a boundary around it.

23
00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:58.970
Quick check!

24
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.370
A single neuron draws which boundary?

25
00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.190
One straight cut.

26
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.250
A closed curve needs the bend,

27
00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.250
and more than one layer.

28
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.190
In the app, open the playground.

29
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.910
Train a small network on a shape

30
00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.050
a line cannot separate, and

31
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.230
watch the boundary bend.

32
00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.230
Your turn.

33
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:24.090
Without an activation, what does

34
00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.470
a stack of layers become?

35
00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:27.550
Remember this.

36
00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.810
One neuron makes one cut, and depth

37
00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.930
bends the boundary only when an

38
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.170
activation sits between the layers.

39
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.810
Try it on paper tonight.

40
00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.430
Compute one forward step: two inputs,

41
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.010
two weights, a bias, then a ReLU.
